me>NAITO KIMITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUTATSUKI, TAKAMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, TATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWANISHI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAZAWA, SHIN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAITO, KIMITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Based on at least one of gene sequence data having been input, a gene motif is extracted. Based on the thus extracted motif, gene sequence data containing this motif are detected from gene sequence data having been clarified. Next, the thus detected gene sequence data are added to the gene sequence data having been input, thereby elevating the gene motif extraction efficiency.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne l'extraction d'un motif génique qui se fonde sur au moins une donnée de séquence géniques ayant été entrée. En fonction du motif ainsi extrait, les données de séquences géniques contenant ce motif sont détectées à partir des données de séquences géniques ayant été clarifiées. Ensuite, les données de séquences géniques ainsi détectées sont ajoutées aux données de séquences géniques ayant été entrées, ce qui augmente l'efficacité de l'extraction du motif génique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>